//! lint:alias ui
//! lint:off scope-balance: ImGui provider - begin*/end* here are the API definitions/forwarders, not paired usage.
// src/ui.zig - immediate-mode UI port, ImGui-style.
// Adapted from Dear ImGui by Omar Cornut, MIT license. Render path
// adapted from rlImGui by Jeffery Myers, zlib license. See
// THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for full attribution and copies.
// scope (THIS file at this state in the project):
//   - Data shape: UiContext (lives in App), Ui handle (per Frame),
//     Window (persistent per-title), Style, plus the geometry
//     primitives borrowed from src/types.zig.
//   - ID stack (FNV-1a hashed) - disambiguates widgets sharing labels.
//   - Layout cursor - widgets advance it; sameLine keeps it on row.
//   - Hit-test + active item state machine - the foundation under
//     every interactive widget.
//   - Internal draw primitives - drawRectFilled / drawRect / drawText
//     routed through rlgl's immediate-mode (rlBegin/rlVertex2f/etc.).
//   - One widget: button. Proves the architecture end-to-end.
//   - Window opens/closes via the optional-handle pattern:
//        if (ui.window("Stats",.{})) |w| {
//            defer w.close();
//            if (ui.button("Reset",.{})) state.counter = 0;
//        }
// What's NOT in (intentionally - see docs/ui-design.md):
//   - More widgets (brings the seven essentials)
//   - Window resize / drag-to-move / collapse
//   - Multi-window z-ordering (current impl just uses submission order)
//   - Style push/pop stacks (per-widget opts cover the needs)
//   - Popups, menus, tab bars, child regions (later phases)
//   - Tables, docking, multi-viewport (out of scope entirely)

